2026-09-16T15:04:19.477133Z [] {'tender_id': None, 'source_reference_id': None, 'source_id': None, 'title': None, 'issuing_agency': None, 'category': None, 'status': None, 'publish_date': None, 'closing_date': None, 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': None, 'location': None, 'description': '', 'contact_name': None, 'contact_email': None, 'contact_phone': None, 'lodgment_address': None, 'documents': [{'file_name': '26AMSA060 - Regional AtoN Maintenance Services - Addendum No 4.txt', 'extracted_text': ' \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nAddendum 3 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nAddendum 3 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nAddendum 3 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nAddendum 2 ? 26AMSA060 \nAddendum 3 ? 26AMSA060 \nAddendum 4 ? 26AMSA060 \nREQUEST FOR TENDER 26AMSA060 - ADDENDUM NUMBER 4 \nREGIONAL ATON MAINTENANCE SERVICES \nThe following information is provided to assist tenderers in responding to RFT 26AMSA060, which \ncloses at, 2:00 PM (Canberra local time) 22 September 2026. \n \nQuestion 1: \nThere are some instances where we have considered a full yearly/2 yearly maintenance visit to a \nremote site to then have a specific maintenance task appear in the next years maintenance list. For \nefficiencies sake can we assume it is ok to bring forward a 5 yearly maintenance task to 4 years to \nalign with the main scheduled maintenance visit? \n \nAnswer 1: \nNo. \nFor clarification and using AN359 Cape Nelson as an example, the Essential Maintenance Activities \nshaded grey below are required to be completed every Site Service (each year). The three other \nEssential Maintenance Activities are required to be completed on each occasion they fall due based \non the Target Start Date and Interval, which in this specific example they will only fall due once during \nthe contract term.  \n \n \nQuestion 2: \nCan AMSA confirm that Statements of Tax records are only required for Tier 1 subcontractors where \nthe value of that subcontract arrangement is estimated to be over $4m (GS-inclusive) \nAnswer 2: \nUnder the Shadow Economy Procurement Connected Policy, Statement of Tax Records (STR) are \nrequired only for first-tier subcontractors whose subcontract is estimated at $4 million or more \n(GST-inclusive).  \n \nQuestion 3: \nAttachment A, Sheet 1.2 lists three separate Essential Maintenance Activities against Region 1 buoy \nsites: "Buoy Replacement", "Buoy Mast Overhaul" and "Buoy Mast Changeout".  \n\n \nProcurement \nAddendum 4 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nThe listed intervals differ: Buoy Replacement at a 16-year interval, and Buoy Mast Overhaul and Buoy \nMast Changeout each at an 8-year interval. At the 16-year point all three activities fall due in the same \nContract Year at the same site.  \na) Where "Buoy Replacement" and the "Buoy Mast Overhaul" / "Buoy Mast Changeout" \nactivities fall due at the same site in the same Contract Year, does Buoy Replacement \nsupersede the concurrent mast activities?  \nb) If the activities are not superseded, can AMSA confirm they are to be priced and delivered \nindependently in the coincident year (i.e. as discrete line items)?  \n \nAnswer 3: \nBuoy Replacement supersedes Buoy Mast Overhaul and Buoy Mast Changeout. \n \nQuestion 4:  \nClause 6.5.5.1 obliges the Contractor to deploy, retrieve, inspect, test, maintain, repair, refurbish and \nreplace floating AtoN and associated mooring systems.  \nClause 6.5.5.10 requires the Contractor to provide an Additional Services quotation covering the \nprocurement, preparation and configuration of buoys and buoy and mooring components required to \ndeliver scheduled Essential Maintenance Activities in the subsequent Contract Year, including "buoy \nand mast components" (6.5.5.10(d)).  \nClause 6.5.5.11(a) provides that, with the exception of the items listed in 6.5.5.10, all other costs for \nEssential Maintenance Activities to buoys are included in the AtoN Maintenance Service Fee.  \na) For Region 1, will AMSA supply replacement buoys, or is the Contractor responsible for \nprocuring them?  \nb) If the Contractor is responsible for procurement, is the cost of a complete replacement buoy \nrecoverable as an Additional Service under clause 6.5.5.10, or is it included within the fixed \nAtoN Maintenance Service Fee under clause 6.5.5.11(a)?  \n \nAnswer 4: \nIf AMSA requires the Contractor to procure buoys or buoy components the Contractor will be \nreimbursed for said procurement in accordance with the provisions of the draft Contract for Additional \nServices or Asset and Spare Parts Purchases. \n \nQuestion 5: \nClause 6.5.5.10 lists buoy and mooring components as Additional Services items ? anodes, mooring \ncomponents, sinkers, buoy and mast components, bolt kits, buoy power supplies (excluding Remote \nMonitors), solar panels, battery cases, mast refurbishment/repainting, mounting brackets and \nassociated freight. Each listed item is a physical component; the verbs used are "procurement, \npreparation and configuration".  \nClause 6.5.5.11(a) places all other Essential Maintenance costs for buoys not listed in 6.5.5.10 within \nthe fixed AtoN Maintenance Service Fee.  \na) Is the Contractor?s labour to prepare and configure buoys ? including installation of power \nsupplies, solar panels, junction boxes, Remote Monitoring, AtoN equipment, antennae, \ncabling, terminations and testing ? recoverable as an Additional Service under clause \n6.5.5.10?  \n \nAnswer 5: \nNo, the Contractors labour is included in the fixed AtoN Maintenance Services Fee. \n\n \nProcurement \nAddendum 4 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \n \nQuestion 6: \nAttachment A, Sheet 1.2 lists the recurring Essential Maintenance Activities for three Region 3 \noffshore reef sites ? AN030 Frederick Reefs, AN389 Saumarez Reefs and AN558 Swain Reefs. At \neach site the substantive maintenance suite (Site Service, Main Lantern Service, Racon Service, \nSolar Power Supply Service, Structure Services, Remote Monitor Service, Lightning Protection \nSystem Service and Third Party Equipment Inspection ? and, at AN558 Swain Reefs, AIS System \nService) carries a 2-year (2.0-year) AtoN Maintenance Interval.  \nThe recorded Target Start Dates are not aligned across the three sites. AN030 Frederick Reefs \ncarries a Target Start Date of 15 October 2027, whereas AN389 Saumarez Reefs and AN558 Swain \nReefs both carry a Target Start Date of 15 October 2028. No timing or alignment comment is \nrecorded against any of these activities.  \na) Can AMSA confirm whether the differing Target Start Dates for AN030 Frederick Reefs (15 \nOctober 2027) versus AN389 Saumarez Reefs and AN558 Swain Reefs (15 October 2028) \nare intentional ? that is, two separate maintenance runs to the reef cluster are to be planned \nand priced in consecutive years?  \n \nAlternatively, are the three sites intended to be combined into a single servicing year, with the \nmaintenance schedule aligned so all three are attended together? If so, can AMSA confirm the \nintended common Target Start Date, so tenderers can price a single mobilisation to the reef cluster?  \na) Will AMSA accept tenderers aligning these three sites to a common servicing cycle (per the \nSite Service Schedule at cl. 5.2.8) for pricing purposes, on the basis that the Annual Work \nForecast and Maintenance Work Program will confirm the actual requirements for each \nContract Year (cl. 6.1.  \n \nAnswer 6: \nThis has been addressed under Addendum 3 Question number 2. AN030 Frederick Reef scheduling \nhas been revised to align with AN558 Swain Reefs and AN389 Saumarez Reefs. Attachment A has \nbeen amended as per below which aligns the Target Start Dates for the three listed sites:  \nRegion \nSite ID \nAtoN Site \nName \nEssential Maintenance Activity \nCompleted \nevery \nEssential \nMaintenance \nSite Visit \nInterval (y) \nTarget Start \nDate \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nRacon Changeout \n8 \nOctober 2030 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nLightning Protection System Service \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nMain Lantern Service \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nRacon Service \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nRemote Monitor Service - Infield \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nSolar Power Supply Service \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nStructure Service - Tower (Brick, Concrete, Ferrous, Lattice, Stone, \nRound (Stainless Steel)) \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nThird Party Equipment Inspection \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nSolar Battery Module Replacement \nSee Note 1 \nOctober 2028 \nRegion 3 \nAN030 \nFREDERICK \nREEFS \nSite Service \nYes \n2 \nOctober 2028 \n \nQuestion 7: \nAN126 Gantheaume Point (Region 7) appears to be identified as requiring a Mains UPS Battery \nReplacement (Attachment A tab 1.4) however it is not clear where a target start date is noted \n(Attachment A tab 1.2). Could you please clarify: \n\n \nProcurement \nAddendum 4 ? 26AMSA060 \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \nProcurement \na) Whether the battery replacement is required during the contract term? \nb) If yes, whether all modules are to be replaced as one activity? \nc) The applicable contract year/target start date? \n \nAnswer 7: \nThis has been addressed in Note to Respondents Number 2 of Addendum number 2. \n \nPlease Note: Further questions may not be accepted after 2.00pm Canberra Local Time,                  \n15 September 2026.  \n \nIssued on 11 September 2026, and authorised by:  \n \n \n \nChris Evans  \nADVISOR PROCUREMENT \nFINANCE AND BUSINESS SERVICES \nCORPORATE SERVICES \n \n \n \n \nChris \nEvans\nDigitally signed \nby Chris Evans \nDate: 2026.09.11 \n16:26:39 +10\'00\'\n\n'}, {'file_name': '26AMSA060 -Addendum No 1 - Regional AtoN Maintenance Services.txt', 'extracted_text': "Procurement \nAddendum 1 ? 26AMSA060\nREQUEST FOR TENDER 26AMSA060 - ADDENDUM NUMBER 1 \nREGIONAL ATON MAINTENANCE SERVICES \nThe following information is provided to assist tenderers in responding to RFT 26AMSA060, which \ncloses at, 2:00 PM (Canberra local time) 22 September 2026. \nNote to respondents No 1 ? Information Package \nAMSA advises that the Tender Information Package referenced in the Approach to Market will be \nmade available for Tenderers to download from 7 August 2026. \nThe Tender Information Package can be accessed from a secure online directory. Tenderers may \nrequest access by emailing contracts-enquiries@amsa.gov.au. AMSA will provide a Tender \nInformation Package Deed of Confidentiality, which must be completed and returned before access \ndetails to the secure online directory are issued. \nNote to respondents No 2 ? Attachment A to Statement of Requirements (Region 3, 6 & 8 \nbuoys) \nAMSA advises that, for Regions 3, 6 and 8, the site service interval is incorrectly stated as 4 years for \nall buoys listed in the Attachment A ? AtoN Site Details tab. Buoys in these regions are included for \nAtoN Fault and Failure Response Services only and do not have any associated Essential \nMaintenance Activities assigned. \nNote to respondents No 3 ? Attachment A to Statement of Requirements (Region 7 buoys) \nAMSA advises that, for Region 7, the site service interval is incorrectly stated as 4 years for all buoys \nlisted in the Attachment A ? AtoN Site Details tab.  Essential Maintenance Activities (and their \ninterval) associated with Buoys in Region 7 are listed in Attachment A ? Essential Maintenance List \ntab. Buoys in Region 7 are also included for the provision of AtoN Fault and Failure Response \nServices. \nIssued on 3 August 2026, and authorised by: \nChris Evans\nADVISOR PROCUREMENT \nFINANCE AND BUSINESS SERVICES \nCORPORATE SERVICES \nChris Evans\nDigitally signed by \nChris Evans \nDate: 2026.08.03 \n14:28:57 +10'00'\n\n"}, {'file_name': '26AMSA060 Regional AtoN Maintenance Services ATM.txt', 'extracted_text': 'Procurement \nApproach to Market 26AMSA060 ? Regional AtoN Maintenance Services \nPage 1 of 33 \n \nApproach to Market \nATM 26AMSA060 \nFor the Provision of Regional Aids to Navigation (AtoN) Maintenance \nServices \n \n \nISSUE DATE: 29 JULY 2026 \nCLOSING TIME & DATE: 2:00pm, CANBERRA LOCAL TIME (AEST) 22 \nSEPTEMBER 2026 \nLODGEMENT ADDRESS: Via AusTender at https://www.tenders.gov.au \n \n\n \nApproach to Market 26AMSA060 ? Regional AtoN Maintenance Services \nPage 2 of 33 \nProcurement \nTable of contents \n1. \nDefinitions ..................................................................................................... 4 \n2. \nIntroduction ................................................................................................... 6 \n2.1 Background to AMSA .................................................................................................... 6 \n2.2 Not Used ....................................................................................................................... 6 \n2.3 Approach to Market ...................................................................................................... 6 \n2.4 Summary of Requirements ........................................................................................... 6 \n2.5 Key Changes from Previous Regional AtoN Maintenance Services Contracts .............. 7 \n2.6 Conditions for Participation ....................................................................................