ng given in clause 2 of Schedule 3.  \nAtoN Network has the meaning given in the Statement of Requirements.  \nAtoN Service Providers means other AtoN service providers other than the Contractor that AMSA \nhas engaged to provide AtoN maintenance and capital works services to AMSA. \nAtoN Site has the meaning given in the Statement of Requirements and as varied by AMSA from \ntime to time in accordance with this Contract.  \nTechnical Support Service Provider has the meaning given in the Statement of Requirements. \nAtoN Freight Services means the services described in clause 4 of Schedule 3. \nAtoN Freight Services Fee means the fee payable for the provision of AtoN Freight Services, as \nspecified in Schedule 4.  \nBackground Material means all material existing at the Effective Date and all material which \ncomes into existence after the Effective Date other than for the purposes of this Contract, and \nwhich is provided to AMSA by the Contractor for the purposes of this Contract, including manuals, \ndocuments, reports, equipment, tools, methodologies, information or other material and data stored \nby any means. \nBusiness Day, means a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public or bank holiday, in: \n(a) \nthe place in which the relevant obligation is to be performed; or  \n(b) \nin the case of an obligation regarding a notice, the place in which the notice is to be \nreceived. \nBusiness Hours means 9am to 5pm on a Business Day. \nComcare means the Australian Government agency known as ?Comcare? or any successor \nagency. \nCommencement Date means 1 July 2027. \nCommonwealth means the Commonwealth of Australia. \nConditions of Contract means the Contract clauses 1 to 6 inclusive contained in this document. \nConfidential Information includes information that: \n(a) \nis by its nature confidential; \n(b) \nis designated by AMSA as confidential; \n(c) \nthe Contractor knows or ought to know is confidential;  \nbut does not include information which:  \ni. \nis or becomes public knowledge, other than by breach of this Contract or any \nother unlawful means;  \nii. \nis in the possession of the Contractor without restriction in relation to \ndisclosure before the date of receipt from AMSA; or \niii. \nhas been independently developed or acquired by the Contractor as \nestablished by written evidence. \n?Consumable? means materials, supplies and items that are used, installed or expended during \nthe performance of the Services including but not limited to items such as or similar to fasteners, \nsealants, lubricants, tapes, adhesives, cleaning materials and are not an Asset or Spare Part. \n\n \n \n \n \n \nContract 26AMSA060 \nAMSA and Organisation Name \n \nPage 6 of 58 \n \nContract means the following documents in the order of precedence below.  In the event of any \ninconsistency between the Contract documents, the following order of precedence will be applied:  \n(a) \nthe Conditions of Contract; \n(b) \nthe Statement of Requirements in Schedule 2, including any attachments to the \nStatement of Requirements; \n(c) \nthe Schedules to this Contract other than the Statement of Requirements; \n(d) \nany other documents incorporated by reference. \nThe Contractor\'s Tender will form part of this Contract but only to the extent required to clarify any \nambiguity, provide evidence for any dispute or rebut any assertion made by the Contractor \ninconsistent with its Tender.   \nContract Manager means the Contractor Personnel specified in Item 4 of Schedule 1, or their \nauthorised delegate or such other person acting in the Contract Manager?s role as notified by the \nContractor from time to time.  \nContract Material means all Material: \n(a) \nbrought into existence for the purpose of performing the Contract Services; \n(b) \nincorporated in, supplied or required to be supplied along with the Material referred \nto in paragraph (a); or \n(c) \ncopied or derived from Material referred to in paragraphs (a) or (b).  \nCont