n \n \nMoAD-Interp Signage Schedule \n00 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nMoAD Graphic Schedule \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nMoAD Mounts Schedule \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nMoAD Style Guide \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nGraphics \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOther  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nDistribution \n Document Type/ Number of Copies \nMoAD ? Tiaan Zapaglione, Shannon Cook  \nE-Em \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nKEY: Document Type \nEg P/3 = Paper Copy/3 copies \nP \nPaper Copy \nD \nDVD CD copy \nE \nElectronic Copy \nO \nOther \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nDelivery Method \n \nH \nHand \nM \nMail \nC \nCourier \nCo \nCollected \nEm \nEmail \nother \n Other as noted \nDB = DropBox \nWT = WeTransfer \nP l e a s e n o t e t h a t M u l l o w a y S t u d i o c a n n o t t a k e a n y r e s p o n s i b i l i t y f o r c h a n g e s m a d e b y o t h e r s t o t h e d o c u m e n t a t i o n . \nI t i s t h e r e s p o n s i b i l i t y o f t h e r e c i p i e n t t o e i t h e r m a r k s u p e r s e d e d o r d e s t r o y e a r l i e r v e r s i o n s o f t h e r e l e v a n t d o c u m e n t . \n \n \n \n3D Approach to Market Package- For Issue \n\n'}, {'file_name': 'Attachment B - 2.1 MoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes.txt', 'extracted_text': ' \n \nMSAOM-LetterStat , Rev 3.0, 01/07/15 \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nDate:  \nTuesday, 18 August 26 \nRef:  \nMoAD01_3D Build- ATM Notes \n \n \nRe: Main KItchen Exhibition- 3D Build Package:  \nSupply + Install- APPROACH TO MARKET ISSUE \nPlease find attached drawings and details for 3D joinery showcase, furniture and signage elements for a \npermanent exhibition for a quotation.  The building and its fabric is a National Heritage Listed item, The \nMuseum of Australian Democracy (MoAD) has detailed prescriptive requirements for managing the extant \nfabric. The installation will need to take this into account, including avoiding damage to heritage \nequipment within the space, in particular the Main Kitchen area. \nThis package is outlined in the accompanying documents as scheduled in the Document Transmittal. Key \nelements include \n? \nnew object display cases  \n? \nframed vitrine case to hot press ( note this equipment contains asbestos material \n? \nbarrier plinth units \n? \nbarrier railing \n? \nframed interpretive signage stands.   \n? \nfixed custom furniture \n? \nloose custom furniture \n? \nother as noted \nThe attached documentation is preliminary and subject to change in finalising the package. Fabricators \nshall allow for joinery lighting where indicated, coordination with graphics, building in AV equipment and \nelectrical supply, as well as prototyping selected elements as noted in the schedules. \nA contingency should be included to allow for changes and refinement of the developed design. \n \n \nDOCUMENT CONTROL \nISSUE  \nDATE  \nDESCRIPTION  \nWRITTEN  \nCHECKED  \nSTATUS  \n00 \n18 Aug 2026 \nIssued for ATM Pricing \nFS \n \nIssued to MoAD \n01 \n \n \n \n \n \n02 \n \n \n \n \n \n03 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 2 of 7 \nGENERAL 3D JOINERY FABRICATION NOTES: \n \n1. PERMANENT EXHIBIT- GENERAL NOTES \na) The exhibition is a permanent exhibition.  \nb) It is likely to remain in this location for approximately 10 years.   \nc) \nInstallation complete shall be fit for purpose. \nd) The building and its fabric, including kitchen equipment is a National Heritage Listed item.  Do not \ndisturb, penetrate or Do not disturb, penetrate or fix to existing surfaces of the heritage building \nwithout prior approval.  \ne) All floors are uneven. The painted concrete Corridor floor has some divots and patchy areas. The \nOrientation Room has an uneven vinyl floor. The MoAD Main Kitchen has a particularly sloping \nfloor to drains- approx 50mm TBC. Allow for adjustable feet or as approved levelling to suit.  \nf) \nAccess to some spaces in the building are restricted with limited widths for some doorways. It is \nanticipated that larger showcases and longer elements may need to be fully demountable and \nflat-packed for assembly on site  due to access limitations  \n2. STANDARDS + CODES \na) All work shall meet required Australian Standards NCC-Building Code requirements- including \nFire Performance. \nb) Framed elements shall be fabricated to avoid potential entrapment. \nc) \nTables shall maintain clearances to AS1428.2 for accessibility. \nd) Off-gassing of all materials is be in accordance with MoAD guidelines and timeframes ? refer \nattached schedule. \n3. LIAISON \na) There are a number of details that will require liaison with the MoAD and Design teams before \nfabrication, with some preparing and developing of prototypes expected- refer selected items as \nscheduled.  Time should be factored in to the price to allow for this. In particular testing the \nstability of vertical elements, and refining the proposed means of jointing + fixing or restraining \nthe individual elements shall be discussed and agreed with the MoAD and Design teams. \nb) Various AV and electrical items will also need to be accommodated in the joinery.  Allow time to \ncoordinate accommodation of the supplied items to be built in where needed.  \nc) \nGraphics packages are still in development- there may be panels that will need to be supplied to \nthe graphics/ signage contractor for printing, prior to fitting within the cabinet.  An indication of \nwhere graphics require coordination with the 3D build is indicated in the schedules.  A preliminary \nschedule of the proposed graphic panels will be provided in due course.  Where indicated to have \nthe base panels made by the 3D joinery fabricator, these shall be panels made to size, delivered \nto the graphics contractor and then returned for final fitting within the cabinet. Other installations \nmay require coordination for final fitting off following graphic panel install by others. \nd)  There are various other acrylic and metal fabricated specialist mounts will be made by others, \nwith some liaison required to ensure a coordinated exhibition cabinet. \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 3 of 7 \n4. NOTES ON THE DOCUMENTATION \na) The Drawings and Specification are to be read in conjunction with the overall ATM package. \nb) The Drawings and Specification represent generally the forms, dimensions and descriptions of \nthe Works.  The layouts as shown on the Drawings are diagrammatic only.  The Fabricator shall \nobtain measurements and other information necessary to carry out the Work. \nc) \nFigured dimensions shall be taken in preference to scaled dimensions.   \nd) Drawings made to larger scales and those showing particular parts of the Works shall take \nprecedence over drawings made to smaller scales and those for more general purposes. \ne) All dimensions shall be confirmed on site by the Fabricator before proceeding. \nf) \nWhere a conflict of information occurs between documents and/or site conditions, the Fabricator \nshall notify the MoAD nominated person immediately for a direction before proceeding. \ng) The Fabricator shall consult the MoAD nominated person with respect to any documentation \nambiguity or omission. Any item which is usual, or necessary, or is reasonably inferred but not \nspecifically documented, shall be deemed to be included in the Contract. \nh) All items either indicated on the Drawings or written in the Specification is to be included, whether \npartially or completely . \ni) \nThe substitution of any item whether of similar or equal quality or utility requires formal written \napproval before proceeding.   \nj) \nNotwithstanding that such items may not be particularly mentioned in this Specification or shown \non Drawings, all fixings are to be in accordance with best trade practice and usage, and other \nfixings which are obviously necessary for the proper completion of the works shall be provided. \n5. QUALITY + WORKMANSHIP \na) Fabricators shall have demonstrated experience in museum exhibition joinery fabrication. \nb) A high museum quality joinery finish is required and the standard of workmanship shall be that of \nan experienced cabinet-maker. \nc) \nAll exposed faces shall be face grade quality. \n6. MATERIALS \na) Cabinets and walls shall be constructed from ?EO? zero-emission MDF or A face-marine grade \nhoop pine with low emission adhesive.   \nb) Hoop Ply is to be utilised for partition walling to reduce item weight. \nc) \nConsider overall weight and durability for transport when finalising carcass thickness. \nd) Pencil round all exposed edges and corners. \ne) Allow for neutral cure silicone seal to all non-bonded junctions, and internal on showcase trims. \nf) \nFinish generally to MDF or PLY be 2-pack finish unless noted otherwise.  \nCases: All rear, floor, base, and dress panels to be EO MDF, with 2pac polyurethane pain finish \non all faces as specified on drawings (fully sealed)  \nDress Panel: Orientation Room large showcases to have 18mm thick solid rear panels, with \n12mm dress panels fixed to rear panels via split battens to allow for fixings of mounts and \nshelving. Align all panel joints with showcase doors. \nTo plinth joinery strip allow to refinish in spray/low nap roller selected enamel paint finish \nTube Rail and selected steelwork ? Dulux Micacious Bridge Paint  \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 4 of 7 \ng) Finish/ Colours:  \nColours are to be advised.  The finalised colour schedule is as below.  \n2-pack paint finish \nx = existing \nP1 \n \n \n \nP2 \n \n \n \nP3 \n \n \n \nEnamel paint finish \nx = existing \nP1A \n \n \nLow nap roller finish \nP2A \n \n \n \nP3A \n \n \n \nOther paint finish \nx = existing \nM1 \n \n \nMicaceous Paint Finish \nPC \n \n \nPowdercoat finish \n \n \n \n \nLaminate finish x = existing \nLAM1 \n \nPrefinished board \nColour TBA   \nLAM-2 \n \nHPL laminate applied \nto substrate \nColour TBA   \nFabric \nUpholstered \nFurniture \n \n \nJoiner to fit \nGraphic Panel types \nG1 \nWrapped vinyl graphic with sandtex finish on aluminium panel. \nG2 \nWrapped vinyl graphic with sandtex finish on MDF panel. \nG3 \n3mm dilite or similar aluminium composite panel with graphic print to face \nG4 \nDirect Stick 1mm PVC printed graphic pane with sandtex finish \nG5 \nfaced rigid foam  signage board with applied graphic vinyl wrap \nG6 \nDirect stick vinyl lettering \nh) Steel framing to furniture and joinery railings ? Pencil round free edges where welded - all welds \nground smooth.   Grub screw joint connectors where shown.  \ni) \nUpholstered items- Commercial quality generally- Fire ratings to NCC.  \nUpholstered seat sofa :  \nFormed foam cushions to seat and rear and backing cushions to be high density commercial \ngrade HD foam as Dunlop Enduro Support (Ignition resistant to AS/NZS 3744.1) with 25mm \nDacron padding overlay.   \nSeat and backing cushions to be fabric upholstered with double seam construction. Commercial \ngrade fabric  as Warwick or equal. Cushion coverings to be removable with zip to concealed \nlocation. Cushions to be secure Velcro or similar attachment to base and rear, and be removable.  \nj) \nProvide means of adjustment to cater for changes in floor level. Provide adjustable skid feet to \nmovable joinery. \nk) \nFor cabinet/case materials allow sufficient time for off-gassing prior to placement of artefacts by \ncurators (refer MoAD specifications).   \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 5 of 7 \n7. ACRYLIC FIXTURES \na) All vitrine cases are to be min 6mm acrylic of a high quality museum grade finish- of thickness to \nsuit the span, loading and application.  Finished acrylic units shall have  ?no bubbles? through \njoint or any visual imperfections.  Top and side edges are to have polished pencil round ?no \nbubbles? through joint and radius. Formed corners or folds where indicated shall be pencil \nrounded and polished.   \nb) All cabinet doors, where acrylic, are to be 10mm acrylic of a high quality museum grade finish \ngenerally.  Finished acrylic units shall have  ?no bubbles? through joint or any visual \nimperfections.  Top, bottom and side edges are to have polished pencil round ?no bubbles? \nthrough joint and radius.   \nNote: Glass alternatives will be considered. \nc) \nAll acrylic formed shelving are to be 6mm acrylic of a high quality museum grade finish.  Finished \nacrylic units shall have  ?no bubbles? through joint or any visual imperfections.  Top, bottom and \nside edges are to have polished pencil round ?no bubbles? through joint and radius. \nd) All shelves shall be removable ? but shall be fixed in place. \ne) Provide new shelves shall be made where required, to match existing.  New shelves will require \nshelving brackets \nf) \nVitrine to hot press is made of large boxed and panel sections. An indicative proposal is included \nin the documents. Allow to fine-tune and refine fabrication detailing in consultation with the MoAD \nand Design teams.  \nThe vitrine shall be fully sealed, and be removable.  The  acrylic panels and boxed sections need \nto be installed with full seals to protect against asbestos containing object within, however it also \nneeds to be removable for 6 monthly periodic inspections. Means of achieving the seal to be \nfinalised with the Design team- but may involve a combination of sealant, brush seals and/or \nscrew fixing to the framed T-type sub-frame.  The base of the vitrine sits upon a steel ledge fixed \nto the base angle to allow for sloping floor. \ng) Pre-drill any required penetrations. \n8. GLASS \na) All glazing shall comply with NCC code and relevant AS glazing standards and safety \nrequirements. \nb) All glass to be min10.38 laminated low iron float glass (mitred as standard), flat polished and \nchamfered - if used for showcase doors. \nc) \nPolish all free edges. \nd) Pre-drill any required penetrations. \ne) Allow for neutral cure silicone bonded joints  \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 6 of 7 \n9. HARDWARE \na) Confirm all hardware selections prior to ordering.  Equal approved alternatives will be considered.  \nb) Provide floor level adjustment as noted  [note: Main Kitchen has a sloping floor to drains, other \nareas are uneven as noted. \nc) \nAllow for satin or satin stainless steel fittings throughout- unless noted otherwise \nd) All locks to be keyed alike- to match existing MoAD locks \ne) Tall Showcase: Hinged glass/ acrylic doors are required to new showcase doors- (as Designcraft  \ntype museum display cases).  Glass/Acrylic doors to be fully openable with fully concealed dual \naction concealed pivot hinges with 110-degree full door opening in carrier rails to top and bottom \nof doors, Integrated lock to MoAd MKeying. Provide bumper/striking plate to opening edge. Tops \nto be glass diffusers with black comcork cover for lighting, with removable clear acrylic top over . \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nf) \nCantilever shelves to be supported on shelf supports.  In addition include pin supports to side \nfront edges of 300 and 400 deep shelves. \n \n \n \n \ng) All acrylic shelves to be secured to brackets in approved manner \nh) AV, Projection and Audio Equipment. Where shown on drawings, Digital AV screens or audio \nhearing cups and associated equipment are to be built into the joinery, and be concealed \nmounted.  Allow for adequate ventilation where electrical equipment. \nDigital AV screens where built in shall be removable for servicing and supported by a cradle \nmount, and accommodate electrical/data connections. Allow to develop and refine these \nelements as part of the design resolution with the MoAD and Design teams.  \nAudio cups are to be mounted to sides of frames as shown \nProjector + mounts to be supplied by others xxx. Provide cable caps where wiring/plugs enter \nMDF/Ply joinery units. \nDetails of equipment to be supplied. Final connections to DIgital screens and AVequipment will \nbe by others after cabinets installed on site.  \ni) \nLighting- Allow to build in lighting to joinery where scheduled. \nj) \nCheck and adjust existing fittings for correct operation. \n10. ELECTRICAL + AV EQUIPMENT \na) Allow for electrical equipment to be installed in cabinets where noted with concealed wiring to \ncurrent codes.   \nb) All wiring to be tagged and ready to plug into supplied power adjacent. \nc) Allow to vent cabinets with electrical  and AV equipment indicated. \nd) AV and Audio Equipment. Where shown on drawings, Digital AV screens or audio hearing cups \nand associated equipment are to be built into the joinery.  Details of the equipment will be \nsupplied to the Fabricator.   \ne) Allow for penetrations for electrical equipment to be installed by others in cabinets where noted \nwith concealed wiring to current codes. Wiring to be concealed within steel frames, other areas to \nbe in concealed location, or neatly placed and fixed in place. Coordinate locations with MoAD \nand Design team. \nf) \nAll wiring to be tagged and ready to plug into supplied power adjacent. (by others) \n\n \nMoAD01_00_260818 3D Build- ATM Notes \nPreliminary ?- Rev 00- Issue 18 Aug 2026 \nPage 7 of 7 \n11. SHOP DRAWINGS + DETAILS \na) Provide Shop Drawings of all fabricated 3D elements, clearly showing sizes, materials, fixings, \nhardware and the like, including all finishes. \nb) Shop Drawings to be submitted for Approval prior to fabrication. Allow 10 business days for \nfeedback and approval. Revise shop drawings based on feedback provided and resubmit for final \napproval. \nc) \nProvide 10 business days for confirmation of any colours or finishes not provided in Fabrication \nissue documentation. \n12. AS-BUILT + ASSEMBLY DETAILS \na) Provide As-Built details of all finishes and hardware used in the final finished product on \ncompletion. \nb) Provide details of all assembly and dis-assembly requirements for the installed joinery and to run \nthrough the process with the MoAD team on completion.  \n\n'}, {'file_name': 'Attachment C - 2.2 MoAD01_00-Showcase Joinery Schedule.txt', 'extracted_text': 'Main Kitchen Exhibition\nMuseum of Australian Democracy\nMoAD-Showcase Joinery Schedule ? Preliminary\nMulloway Studio\nMoAD-Showcase Joinery Schedule-\n Revision 00- Pricing Issue- 18 Aug 2026\n1\n3D  build- Showcase/ Joinery Units\nAll materials and installation to comply with NCC.\nCoordinate and finalise details with Design team.\nAll shall allow adjustability for uneven floor level- \nadjustable feet or other as agreed\nCode\nn? off\nType\n room number/ \nlocation \n width \n(mm) \n depth \n(mm) \nheight \n(mm)\nmaterial/ frame \nfinish\nelec / additional\nnotes\nimpact to existing \nbuilding\nGraphic \nNo.\nimage\nJ.01\n1\nTable-\ninteractive\n LF509 \n3300\n300-890\n700.0\n30mm MDF benchtop with 20 SHS mitre jointed and welded framing\nFormed casing about integrated touchscreen with concealed \nsupporting cradle. Allow access to AV\ncable cap as needed. Adjustable feet\nMDF: 2-pack paint finish\nSteel frame :Micaceous paint- \nspray finish\n32" touch screen + driver, \ncables\nTo allow for install and access to AV equipment- \nprovide internal cradle. Fframing + blocking as \nrequired, provide rear access to AV equipment for \nmaintenance.Allow for venting of equipment- possible\nperforated mesh backing to AV cradle\n top aligns with adjacent J.01.\nClearances to AS1428.2\nallow to build in as free \nstanding element\nyes\nJ.02\n1\nBench/Sofa\n LF509 \n1960\n500\n800/ 700 \narmrests\nBase: 30mm MDF base with vent holes\nBacking and Table Arms: 16mm MDF\nFraming: 20 SHS mitre jointed and welded framing\nUpholstery Commercial grade HD foam cushions to seat and rear,  \nfabric upholstered with double seam. Cushions to be attached to base, \nand be removable. Cushion coverings to be removable\nAdjustable feet\nMDF: 2-pack paint finish\nSteel frame :Micaceous paint- \nspray finish\nProvide upholstered cushions to all seating elements \nto extent as shown on drawings. No \nsharp corners or protrusion of base past cushion\nTable rest top aligns with adjacent J.01.\nallow to build in as free \nstanding element\nJ.03\n1\nBookshelf \n LF509 \n1000\n300\n700\n30mm MDF top  16mm MDF generally \nmitre joints generally,pencil round where edges exposed.\nAngled display  to upper shelf\nAllow 50mm skirting. Adjustable feet\nMDF: 2-pack paint finish\nallow min 20mm to sides and top \nkeep clear of adjacent \nsurfaces and fitures to \nsides\nJ.04\n2\nRecipe Rail\n LF509 \n2580\n16mm MDF backing panel with 2 off anodised aluminium docket rails \nto full width ( 2 per length/ total 4)\nMDF: 2-pack paint finish\nstrap fix on side to existing column\nside clamp fix to existing \ncolumn to MoAD \nrequirements\nyes\nJ.05\n1\nHotpress vitrine LF509 \n3600\n1200\n1100\nSteel Frame: 20 SHS with welded T piece\nVitrine:  Acrylic panels with fully welded with pencil rounded corners to \ntop and end side edges. Pre-drill at fixing locations. Panles to be \nremovable for cleaning and curator access. Polish exposed corners \nand free edges.\nSteel Base Angle: 120x90 angle to base with supporting ledge at rake \nto allow vitrine to site level on angled floor.\nSeals: Allow for fully dust sealed enclosure.  \nSteel frame + Base angle \n:Micaceous paint- spray finish\nAsbestos contining equipment within case\nvitrine to be fully sealed with silicon. brush seals or \nother agreed. Positive screw fixings to T bar sections.\nRound off and polish edges (no sharp corners)\nAll panels to be removable for 6 monthly periodic \ncleaning and inspections- Coordinate and fianlise \ndetails with Design team.\nJ.06\nin \ndivisions Showcase\n LF519 \narea: 7m2\nnorth: 550\nangled \ncorner: \nnom 950\nwest: 480\n2200\nMuseum Grade case ( Designcraft type or equal) \nCarcass: Nom 20mm MDF with Hoop Pine to rear. Mitre joints \ngenerally. Tall skirting piece with blocking as needed\nVitirne/Doors: Min 10mm toughened clear glass with concealed pivot \nhinges in carrier rails to top and bottom of doors, Integrated lock to \nMoAd MKeying. (Glass door w nom 1000mm)\nFixed glass vitrine windows where shown,\nTop: Glass diffusers with black comcork cover for case lighting over, \nwith removable clear acrylic top over -  T-bar or similar support frame- \nlihting over.\nDress Panel: 18mm thick solid rear panels, with 12mm dress panels \nfixed to rear panels via split battens to allow for fixings of mounts and \nshelving. Align all panel joints with showcase doors\nShelving:  Cantilevered Glass  to locations as shown- or acrylic folded \nshelves with label to front.-extent TBC-\nAllow  to cooridinate works to allow for installation of rear graphic \npanel before fitting off fixtures, shelving, object mounts and standing \npin/rod type mounts. \nBase plinth inside case  with angled frontal to carry story graphic- \nextent TBC\nPlinth blocks for objects- number and array TBC- \nAllow to level for uneven floor.\nMDF: 2-pack paint finish\ncase lighting overhead\npossible internal lighting- TBC\nTop of showcase (glass) to allow overhead  lighting \nfixture-  conceal drivers and wiring , \nCoordinate with object and graphic layouts to provide \nrequired mountingand fixing locations as required