xtracted_text': 'Page | 70 \nAppendix B Exhibition Material Specifications \n \n \nNot to be used X\nShowcase \nConstruction \nMDF\nUrea formaldehyde \nZeroE MDF\nPlywood (Marine, or exterior grade) with a \nphenol formaldehyde base  this is classified for \nexternal use, as it \nin the presence of water. \nHoop Pine - solid, or ply with phenol \nformaldehyde adhesive. \nPolyurea based wood adhesives (also called \nzero- formaldehyde) are also OK. \nPaints \nOils and alkyd-based binders not suitable \n(release formic acid). Latex paints only to be \nused over a pre-existing barrier coating or \nlaminate. \nMoisture-cured polyurethanes are not \nacceptable for health reasons. \nHigh VOC paints should not be used. \npaints such as water-based emulsion paints with\nacrylic binders (i.e. ECO, Dulux Breath Easy). \n \n-gassing minimum of 4\ndays for zero VOC paints. \n-gassing of 14 days \nfor zero VOC paints. \nSealants\nNeutral-cure silicone sealants must be applied at \nleast 14 days before object installation. \nTextiles \nNo velvet, wool, silk, suede (or artificial \nsuede) to be used. \nCotton, polyester, linen OK. \n \nMounting systems\nIf mount is not conservation grade\nmaterials it should be covered/sealed with \nconservation grade materials i.e. silicone \ntubing \nPE, PP, acrylic or polyester plastics, silicone,\nstainless steel, acid free paper products. \nAdhesives \nSolvent based adhesives e.g. contact \ncement \n3M hot melt adhesive \nAcrylic emulsion (EVA?) \nPolyvinyl acetate (PVA) requires minimum 4 \nweeks off-gassing \nGraphic panels   \nVinyls \nNothing with PVC (polyvinyl chloride) \nPE, PP or polyester plastics \nInks\nMust off-gas for 7 days before being installed \ninto a showcase containing objects.  \n \n \n \n \nEnglish Heritage has developed a decision support tool for Showcase off-gassing. \n \nUpdated MEMORI decision support tool  \n \n \n \n\n'}, {'file_name': 'Attachment G - 3.1 MoAd01 260818 DD Main Kitchen-for pricing issue.txt', 'extr