tive Colour on Elevation ? Clarification \n\n \n \nOFFICIAL \nOFFICIAL \nA) Indicative colour has been used to indicate surface finish. Refer also to the full \ndocument package. \na. Yellow: Graphic to substrate \nb. Cyan: Plinth Joinery \nCC4. J.02 Bench / Sofa ? Amended detail \nA) Rear cushion to be 50mm thick and tapered to seat cushion. \nCC5. Drawing MoAD01-DD-1-1-JS ? Clarification \nA) P1-xxx indicates the overall length of plinth assembly excluding corner units. \nCC6. J.06 Showcase ? Amended Drawing MoAD01-DD-5-0-J Rev A \nA) Reduce the height of skirting to align existing joinery. Provide 32mm chrome \nplated CHS column with collar to each max 1200mm. \nB) Add more shelving for objects. Refer details on attached Amended Drawing \nMoAD01-DD-5-0-J. Rev A. This drawing has been reissued to clarify the structural \nframing and additional shelving for objects. \nCC7. J.12 Armchair ? Addition \nA) Add two J.12 Armchair in front of J.01, as Refer to Drawing MoAD01-DD-7-1-J and \nDD-7-2-J \nCode \nn? \noff \nType \nroom \nnumber \n/location \nwidth \n(mm) \ndepth \n(mm) \nheight \n(mm) \nmaterial/ \nframe \nfinish \nJ.12 \n2 \nArmchair \nLF509 \n500 \n500 \n800 \nAs J.02 \n As J.02 \n \n \n\n'}, {'file_name': 'MoAD-ATM-7624 RFI - 4 September 2026.txt', 'extracted_text': " \n \nOFFICIAL \nOFFICIAL \nMoAD-ATM-7624 \nRFIs \nPublished Friday 4 September 2026 \n \nQ1. Regarding the hot press and the access required for maintenance, are you \nproposing a series of removable panels or one large panel? \n A1. The current design documentation shows a light and steel subframe with separable \nacrylic panels. The intention is that the steel frame itself might remail in place, while the \nacrylic panels can be removed as required. The acrylic panels only need to be removed \nfor cleaning and preservation purposes approximately every 6 to 12 months. \n \nQ2. Has an official opening date been nominated? \nA2. The exhibition is currently scheduled to be com
